{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;In the absence of an internal daylight and sunlight assessment, the proposal is considered likely to fail to provide adequate levels of natural light. In addition, the siting of windows would result in overlooking from the neighbouring garden. As a result, the proposal would fail to provide an acceptable quality of accommodation, detrimental to the living conditions of future occupiers. It is therefore at odds with the following policies which seek to ensure that development proposals provide a high quality of accommodation:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;&quot;&gt;National Planning Policy Framework&amp;nbsp;(December 2023) &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Policy D6 of the London Plan (March 2021) &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Policy CP3 of the&amp;nbsp;Local Development Framework Core Strategy (July 2010) &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Policies BP6 and BP11 of the&amp;nbsp;Local Development Framework Borough Wide Development Plan Document (March 2011)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Policy SP2 of&amp;nbsp;The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan: (Regulation 19 Submission Version, December 2021)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt;&quot;&gt;Housing Design Standards London Plan Guidance (GLA, June 2023)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development would introduce a residential dwelling to a rear garden setting with associated increase in noise, general disturbance and overlooking. This would detract from the amenity value of the surrounding rear gardens, to the detriment of the living conditions of neighbouring occupiers. The proposal is therefore found to be at odds with the following policies which seek to ensure that development proposals maintain residential amenity:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;&quot;&gt;National Planning Policy Framework&amp;nbsp;(December 2023) &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Policies GG3, D6 (Part D) and D14 of the London Plan (March 2021)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Policies BP8 and BP11 of the&amp;nbsp;Local Development Framework Borough Wide Development Plan Document (March 2011)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Policies DMD1 and DMSI3 of&amp;nbsp;The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan: (Regulation 19 Submission Version, December 2021)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;",
    "&lt;p style=&quot;&quot;&gt;The proposed development, by reason of siting and design, would disrupt the surrounding pattern of development and would be at odds with the character of the surrounding dwellings. It therefore fails to represent a high quality design, and would have a detrimental impact on the character and appearance of the surrounding area. The proposal thus fails to comply with the following policies which seek to ensure development proposals are sympathetic to local character and appearance:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;&quot;&gt;National Planning Policy Framework&amp;nbsp;(December 2023) &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Policy D4 of the London Plan (March 2021) &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Policy CP3 of the&amp;nbsp;Local Development Framework Core Strategy (July 2010) &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Policy BP11 of the&amp;nbsp;Local Development Framework Borough Wide Development Plan Document (March 2011)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Policies SP2 and DMD1 of&amp;nbsp;The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan: (Regulation 19 Submission Version, December 2021)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;",
    "&lt;p style=&quot;&quot;&gt;The proposed development fails to demonstrate&amp;nbsp;that additional demand for parking from the development could be adequately accommodated in the surrounding area. In addition, it fails to provide safe and suitable access to the new dwelling, resulting in vehicular and pedestrian conflict. The proposal is therefore likely to add unacceptably to parking stress and congestion in the vicinity of the application site, and to have a negative impact on highway safety.&amp;nbsp; As such, it fails to comply with the following policies&amp;nbsp;which seek to ensure that proposals show how car parking will be designed and managed, to take into consideration on-street parking availability and existing and planned public transport provision, and to not negatively impact highway safety : &lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;&quot;&gt;National Planning Policy Framework&amp;nbsp;(December 2023) &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Policies T1, T6.1 and D5 of the London Plan (March 2021)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;Policy CP3 of the&amp;nbsp;Local Development Framework (LDF) Core Strategy (July 2010)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Policies&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;BP8 , BP11, BR9 and&amp;nbsp;BR11&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;of the&amp;nbsp;Local Development Framework Borough Wide Development Plan Document (March 2011) &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Policies SP2, SP8 and DMT2 of&amp;nbsp;The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan: (Regulation 19 Submission Version, December 2021)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;"
  ],
